{\large\bfseries Application for Product Analytics Manager - Customer Retention \& Expansion (m/w/d), at Conceptboard}

\vspace{25pt}

Berlin, Germany, 27.05.2026

\vspace{15pt}

Dear Hiring Team,

\vspace{10pt}

Conceptboard solves a fundamental friction in digital work: the moment collaboration ends and execution begins. Most teams treat the whiteboard as a temporary space for brainstorming, forcing them to migrate ideas into a separate task management tool where context evaporates. By enabling teams to turn board content into assigned, tracked tasks without leaving the workspace, Conceptboard is building the bridge between creative ideation and project delivery. Scaling this model requires shifting from feature adoption to deep integration, where the whiteboard becomes the primary operating system for a team's workflow.

At FORVIA HELLA, I managed the B2B e-commerce platform for 60,000+ workshop users, where the core challenge was similar: users were comfortable with legacy ordering habits and needed a tangible reason to shift their daily workflow to our digital platform. I redesigned the onboarding experience to anchor retention to repeat digital order rates, implementing in-product guidance that reduced order completion time by 35\% and improved self-service adoption by 40\%. By mapping the drop-off points in our onboarding funnel, I translated behavioral signals into specific triggers for our commercial teams, which directly contributed to €12M+ in Year 1 revenue.

I have spent my career building systems that convert intermittent usage into habitual integration. Whether redesigning checkout funnels to eliminate friction or architecting predictive models to identify engagement decay before it manifests as churn, I focus on the data that predicts long-term value. I am interested in bringing this experience to Conceptboard to help build the early-warning systems and expansion mechanics that turn your active users into long-term organizational partners.


\vspace{20pt}

Kind regards,

\vspace{1pt}

Rodrigo Lopes

